      "summaryMarkdown": "This review supersedes the failed review at revision 4. The rename is clean:\n\n- The moved files differ from their originals only by the mechanical path mapping.\n- No old-meaning `rayx_core`, `rayx::core` or `rayx::app::` remains outside deliberate history.\n- The macros resolve `rayx`, else `rayx_app`, else `rayx_app_nsh`, per d-crate-names.\n- The umbrella exposes `app` and `app_nsh`, and `rayx_app` is NSH-free.\n- CI's wasm step and the library guard match the design.\n\nThe three findings are resolved:\n\n- S1-F1: `rayx_app_nsh` carries a never-matching `git_tag_name` until its first release, asserted in `release_automation` and explained in `docs/releasing.md`.\n- S1-F2: `macro_paths` runs `cargo check` on fixture crates on `rayx_app` alone and on `rayx_app_nsh` alone.\n- S1-F3: the library guard's doc lists `rayx_services_*`.\n\nAll five sprint checks pass at this snapshot. CRATES-2 is supporting here and was judged only for its s1 part. The `refactor!` commit with its `Migration: apps:` footer is still to be made. Memory still names `rayx_core` (task t21).",
